      "explanation": "By definition, \\(\\log_{10}7\\) is the exponent \\(t\\) for which \\(10^t=7\\). The logarithm is defined because its base \\(10\\) is positive and different from \\(1\\), and its argument \\(7\\) is positive. Therefore\n\\[\n10^{\\log_{10}7}=\\boxed{7},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
